@startuml
title Re-Score Sequence — Manual Edit Evaluation (Writer Skipped)

actor User
participant "Job Detail View" as UI
participant "TanStack Query" as TQ
participant "IPC Main" as IPC
participant "Scorer Agent (ATS)" as Scorer
participant "Reviewer Agent (Humanizer)" as Reviewer
participant "Mistral LLM" as LLM

User -> UI : Edit resume manually → click "Re-Score"
UI -> TQ : useMutation: reScore(searchId, jobId, currentContent)
TQ -> IPC : invoke("document:rescore:stream:<id>")

note right of IPC : Writer is SKIPPED — evaluation only

IPC -> Scorer : evaluate(userEditedContent, jobDescription)
Scorer -> LLM : score ATS match
LLM --> Scorer : { atsScore, passed, feedback }
Scorer --> IPC : { type: "score", atsScore }
Scorer --> IPC : { type: "feedback", feedback: [...] }
IPC --> TQ : stream → score panel updates

IPC -> Reviewer : evaluate(userEditedContent)
Reviewer -> LLM : detect AI tells, rate naturalness
LLM --> Reviewer : { humanScore, passed, feedback, suggestions }
Reviewer --> IPC : { type: "score", humanScore }
Reviewer --> IPC : { type: "feedback", feedback: [...] }
Reviewer --> IPC : { type: "personalization", suggestions: [...] }
IPC --> TQ : stream → score panel updates

IPC -> "SQLite" : UPDATE adapted_resumes SET ats_score, human_score, updated_at
IPC --> TQ : { type: "done" }
TQ --> UI : Score panel updates — editor content unchanged
UI --> User : ATS: 88% · Human: 82% — see suggestions below

@enduml
